PATCH 392: twin #3 ROOT -- in-mission VIEW SELECT store-width bug (5d43) that mapped the whole
HANG bucket (AZER2/AZER3 + ~18 *2-7 missions) to the map view + chain-B overrun hang.

Located by a mission-init function-trace diff (AZER1 cockpit vs AZER2 hang): both build the same view
template (5cce->4823->1cdb, word[DGROUP:0x3b3c] = 0x0060 map default), then 5cce's 2ce7-gated FUN_0000_5d43
switches the view node to the COCKPIT element (0x011a) via FUN_0000_44be -- but ONLY if the player-vehicle
gate passes.  The gate `3 < *puVeh` (Ghidra uint*, 4-byte) read word[+0]|word[+2]<<16; the asm `cmp WORD
[di],3` reads only word[+0].  AZER2's vehicle word[+2]=0x0008 -> 0x00080000 > 3 -> wrong `goto 5d7c` ->
44be skipped -> map view -> chain-B hang.  Fix = the faithful WORD compare + BYTE [di+0x16] flag tests.

VALIDATED (native): AZER2 hang->COCKPIT crash-free (rc=0); all 7 landed mission flows (AZER1/CYPRUS1/
SAUDI1/SYRIA1/INDIA1/SAUDI7/AZER7) central-chrome AE=0 unchanged (no regression).  re_out/fist.c pristine.

